      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4455407005": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-11-15T22:56:54.715047+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "About the Company\nCareem is building the Everything App for the greater Middle East — making it easy to move around, order food and groceries, manage payments, and more. Our purpose is simple: to simplify and improve people’s lives and build an awesome organisation that inspires.\nSince 2012, Careem has enabled earnings for over 2.5 million Captains, simplified the lives of more than 70 million customers, and built a platform where the region’s best talent and entrepreneurs thrive. We operate in 70+ cities across 10 countries, from Morocco to Pakistan.\nWe’re now entering our next chapter — one powered by AI. We’re looking for AI talent: curious problem-solvers who know how to apply AI to build tools, automate workflows, and create real impact. Whether it’s streamlining operations, enhancing customer experience, or reimagining internal systems — we want people who can make Careem work smarter and move faster.\nAbout the team\nAt Careem, the mission for the NextGen program is to help grow our new joint Engineering by learning how to write Clean Code, use SOLID principle techniques, and design reliable systems. The ultimate goal is to train the new Engineers to build Engineering excellence foundations with high standards. Our program covers all the areas of Careem tech be it Cyber Security, Data, Infrastructure, and all the Software Engineering tracks like Backend, Frontend as well as Mobile.\nWe are looking for software engineers to join our team of talented engineers that share a common interest in distributed backend systems, their scalability, and continued development. You will work alongside a top talent for an accelerated learning path. You will have access to some of the most exciting projects and advanced tech for accelerated learning and exposure.\nYou will be responsible for maintaining some of our services that power the Careem Engine, scaling highly distributed systems, and continuously documenting and improving our engineering practices. These large-scale, distributed systems handle everything from user requests to payment processing.\nWhat you'll do:\nResponsibilities\nOur tech stack is Java 8 and Spring Boot, Micro-Service Architecture, SQL and no-SQL DBs, and AWS infrastructure. Key responsibilities include:\nDevelopment of our distributed backend system to meet the challenging functional, scalability, and reliability requirements for our fast-growing business.\nMaintain features and systems, with an emphasis on code quality, maintainability, readability, and testing.\nFacilitate collaboration with other engineers, product owners, and designers to solve interesting and challenging problems across our platform.\nBe a valued member of an autonomous, cross-functional agile team.\nYou care about quality and you know what it means to ship high-quality code.\nWhat you'll need:\nFresh graduates are encouraged to apply!\nThe ideal candidate will have a passionate commitment to improving the lives of people, an insane focus on excellence and customer service, and a strong alignment with our core values: being bold, focused, agile and collaborative.\nMust have:\nBachelor's Degree in Computer Science or other related technical fields.\nUnderstanding of Object-oriented design, data structures, and algorithms.\nAbility to solve complex problems.\nMust be able to write clean and maintainable code (must love coding!).\nAbility to effectively articulate technical challenges and solutions; deal with loosely defined problems and fast-changing requirements & think abstractly.\nPassionate about learning new technologies and working on a product of massive scale and impact.\nAble to communicate effectively.\nAttention to detail.\nNice to have:\nKnowledge of AWS\nKnowledge of clean code principles\nDeep understanding of design patterns\nDemonstrated ability of test-driven development",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4474558058": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-11-15T22:56:54.715047+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "About Us\nConsertus is an AI-native global capital program management and advisory firm that combines deep industry expertise with advanced digital capabilities to deliver smarter, faster, and more sustainable outcomes. Headquartered in Miami, Florida, and supported by a team of more than 1,500 professionals , we help clients plan, deliver, and optimize complex capital programs across the full project lifecycle.\nOur integrated capabilities span advisory, digital solutions, engineering and design, and program delivery, enabling organizations to navigate complexity, mitigate risk, and achieve strategic objectives. We serve a diverse range of industries, including aviation, transportation, transit, water, healthcare, energy, education, government, commercial real estate, life sciences, and technology.\nAt Consertus, we believe our people are our greatest strength. We foster a collaborative, flexible, and inclusive environment where individuals can grow, develop their skills, and make a meaningful impact. Together, we're transforming the way the world is planned, built, and delivered.\nLearn more about how Consertus is creating lasting value for clients, communities, and our people at www.consertus.com.\nAbout This Role\nWe are seeking a talented, proactive, and security-conscious Application Developer to join our IT organization. In this role, you will architect, build, optimize, and maintain high-performance Python applications deployed entirely across Google Cloud Platform (GCP).\nYou will leverage Claude Code as your primary AI-assisted development environment to accelerate delivery cycles, enhance code quality, generate comprehensive test suites, and perform rigorous post-build security validations.\nThe ideal candidate blends solid software engineering fundamentals with modern AI-native development workflows, event-driven cloud architecture, and a strong security-first mindset.\nKey Responsibilities\nApplication Development & Architecture\nDesign, develop, test, deploy, and maintain resilient Python applications utilizing Cloud Run, GKE, Cloud Functions, and Compute Engine.\nBuild scalable microservices and event-driven solutions using Cloud Pub/Sub, Cloud Tasks, and Eventarc.\nDevelop and maintain RESTful APIs using FastAPI and gRPC services with robust authentication, versioning, and performance optimization.\nWrite clean, maintainable, modular Python code following PEP 8 standards, static typing practices, and software engineering best practices.\nParticipate in technical design sessions, sprint planning, code reviews, and architecture discussions.\nCloud Infrastructure & DevOps\nDevelop and maintain Infrastructure as Code (IaC) solutions using Terraform.\nConfigure and support CI/CD pipelines utilizing Cloud Build, Artifact Registry, Cloud Deploy, and GitHub Actions.\nImplement monitoring, logging, tracing, and alerting strategies using Google Cloud Monitoring, Cloud Logging, and Cloud Trace.\nSupport enterprise data platforms including BigQuery, Cloud SQL, Firestore, Cloud Spanner, and Cloud Storage.\nAssist in implementing secure cloud architecture practices through IAM, workload identity federation, and least-privilege access controls.\nAI-Assisted Development\nUtilize Claude Code and modern AI coding assistants to accelerate development, refactoring, testing, and documentation efforts.\nDesign effective prompts and workflows that produce reliable, scalable, and production-ready code.\nReview, validate, and enhance AI-generated output to ensure quality, maintainability, and security.\nGenerate automated testing frameworks, OpenAPI documentation, and developer resources using AI-assisted tools.\nSupport adoption of AI-enabled software development life cycle (SDLC) best practices across the technology organization.\nSecurity & Compliance\nConduct application security assessments using tools such as Bandit, Semgrep, Snyk, and SonarQube.\nImplement OWASP-aligned secure coding standards, input validation, and secure API development practices.\nManage secrets and credentials through Google Secret Manager and Cloud KMS.\nEnsure solutions comply with applicable enterprise security standards and regulatory requirements including SOC 2, ISO 27001, and HIPAA when required.\nQualifications/Requirements\nRequired: Fully bilingual in English and Spanish, with professional fluency in speaking, reading, and writing both languages.\nBachelor's degree in Computer Science, Information Technology, Software Engineering, or a related technical field, or equivalent professional experience.\n3 - 5 years of professional software development experience building enterprise applications.\nStrong proficiency with Python 3.10+ and modern application development frameworks including FastAPI.\nExperience with asynchronous programming, object-oriented design principles, and API development.\nExperience designing and deploying containerized applications in Google Cloud Platform environments.\nHands-on experience with Cloud Run, GKE, Cloud Functions, BigQuery, Pub/Sub, Firestore, Cloud SQL, and Cloud Storage.\nExperience developing Infrastructure as Code solutions using Terraform.\nExperience implementing automated testing frameworks with pytest, unittest, or similar tools.\nFamiliarity with CI/CD pipelines and DevOps methodologies.\nExperience working with AI-assisted development tools such as Claude Code, GitHub Copilot, or Cursor.\nPreferred Qualifications\nGoogle Cloud Associate Cloud Engineer or Professional Cloud Developer certification.\nGoogle Cloud Professional Cloud Security Engineer or Professional Cloud DevOps Engineer certification.\nExperience integrating enterprise platforms such as Workday, Salesforce, Deltek Vantagepoint, or Ironclad.\nFamiliarity with Vertex AI, Document AI, Gemini APIs, LangChain, LlamaIndex, or other AI/ML development frameworks.\nExperience with container security, Binary Authorization, Kubernetes security controls, and runtime monitoring solutions.\nContributions to open-source projects, Python packages, or cloud-native development tools.\nStrong understanding of secure software development practices and application security principles.\nWorking Hours\nFull Time; Hybrid or Remote, depending on proximity to a local office.\nHow To Apply\nIf you’re passionate about building secure, scalable cloud applications we’d love to hear from you. Apply today!\nEqual Employment Opportunity Statement\nConsertus is proud to be an Equal Opportunity Employer. We celebrate diversity and are committed to creating an inclusive environment for all employees. We welcome applicants from all backgrounds and identities, and we do not discriminate on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, national origin, disability, age, veteran status, or any other protected status.",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4475045317": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-11-15T22:56:54.715047+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "About FullStack\nFullStack is your AI-native engineering partner, built to turn AI capability into certainty. Most companies can demo AI; few can get it to production and prove what it produced. We close that gap with three capabilities, AI built into your products from the start, elite vetted talent who apply it, and transparent execution that shows value every step of the way. With now over 600 customers in North America, FullStack is one integrated partner for all your AI engineering needs. With FullStack, you move forward with confidence.\nWe’re Most Proud Of\nOffering life-changing career opportunities to talented software professionals across the Americas.\nBuilding highly-skilled software development teams for hundreds of the world’s greatest companies.\nHaving delivered hundreds of successful custom software solutions, which have positively impacted the lives and careers of millions of users.\nOur 4.1-star rating on GlassDoor.\nOur client Net Promoter Score of 68, twice the industry average.\nThe Opportunity\nJoin our talent network and connect with U.S. clients for flexible, project-based development work as an Agentic Software Engineer (Google Antigravity).\nYou will integrate directly into our client's team and work alongside their existing designers and engineers on a daily basis.\nWhat We're Looking For\n5+ years of professional software development experience with a deep understanding of full-stack architectures (e.g., Java, Python, C#, React, Node, etc.).\n1-3 years of professional experience using Google Antigravity as a primary development environment to coordinate AI-driven implementation across large, multi-file systems while maintaining architectural oversight.\nExperience delivering production software where AI systems generate the majority of implementation code.\nStrong context engineering skills, including structuring codebases, specifications, and documentation to produce reliable, context-efficient AI output.\nAbility to translate complex product requirements into machine-executable, AI-friendly specifications.\nExperience designing AI-first development workflows from specification through deployment.\nAbility to systematically improve AI-generated output through structured iteration and feedback loops.\nComfort working across multiple stacks, using AI to deliver high-quality, production-ready systems.\nExperience operating across frontend, backend, and infrastructure in AI-accelerated environments.\nDisciplined human-in-the-loop review practices, with risk-adjusted validation for high-impact or safety-critical flows.\nStrong curiosity and initiative in evaluating and adopting emerging AI-native engineering practices.\nAdvanced understanding of Agile methodologies and Lean principles and participation in team ceremonies as well as asynchronous work.\nAdvanced English is required.\nSuccessful completion of a four-year college degree is required.\nA positive mindset and a can-do attitude.\nAbility to identify with the goals of FullStack's clients and dedicate yourself to delivering on commitments.\nAbility to consistently work 40 hours per week.\nWork Authorization Requirements\nApplicants must be currently authorized to work in the country of this job posting on a full-time basis.\nFullStack will not sponsor applicants for work visas now or in the future.\nWhat We Offer\nCompetitive pay.\n100% remote work.\nThe ability to work with leading startups and Fortune 500 companies.\nContinuing education opportunities.\nOpportunity to grow and expand your career.\nOur talent network is committed to fostering a diverse, inclusive, and accessible environment where IT professionals can find opportunities that match their skills. We welcome individuals of all races, religions, genders, sexual orientations, national origins, abilities, and experiences. Our focus is on connecting talent with projects based on qualifications, ensuring a fair and transparent process that values diverse perspectives and global collaboration.\nLearn more about our Applicants Privacy Notice.",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4475049119": {
