      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4489542233": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-11-15T22:56:54.715047+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "About Ortelan\nOrtelan is an applied AI lab. We build our own AI products, run AI systems for organizations on their own data and infrastructure, and invest in early-stage AI companies. Our products are Praus, an AI assistant for research, writing and code, and Lost Tribes, an AI agent for family research.\nAbout the role\nYou will build the products people use every day. Praus brings research, writing and code into one workspace, with projects, group chats, voice and agents. Lost Tribes searches historical records and builds family trees with the source behind every connection.\nYou will work across the whole stack, from the interface people see to the services that route each request to the right model. You will ship often, see how people use what you built, and decide with the product team what to build next.\nIn this role, you will\nBuild product features end to end, from the interface to the backend\nDesign interfaces for AI products that show their sources, handle uncertainty and stay fast\nBuild the services behind them, including APIs, data models, background jobs and integrations\nWork with model routing, retrieval and agent features alongside our AI engineers\nMake the products fast, reliable and affordable to run\nTalk to users and use what you learn to improve the product\nYou may be a good fit if you\nHave 0 to 3 years of experience building web products, with work you can show us\nWrite production code in TypeScript and are comfortable with React and a backend language such as Node or Python\nCare about how a product feels to use, down to the details\nHave built something with language models, or want to\nWork well remotely and set your own direction\nStrong candidates may also have experience with\nReal-time features such as streaming, chat or collaboration\nPostgres, queues and cloud infrastructure\nShipping AI features in a consumer or business product\nStartups, side projects or open-source work\nWe encourage you to apply even if you do not meet every qualification listed here. We care most about what you have built.\nLocation\nThis role is remote within the United States, with occasional visits to our Salt Lake City office.\nCompensation\nThe annual base salary range for this role is $0 to $150,000. Individual compensation is determined by job-related skills, experience and location. The role is also eligible for a performance bonus.\nHow to apply\nApply via LinkedIn. You can learn more about our work at ortelan.com.\nEqual employment opportunity\nOrtelan is an equal opportunity employer. We do not discriminate on the basis of race, religion, color, national origin, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, age, veteran status, disability, genetic information, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law. Qualified applicants with arrest or conviction records will be considered for employment in accordance with applicable law.",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4489544014": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-11-15T22:56:54.715047+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "About The Role\nEnterprises of all sizes trust Abnormal AI’s cloud products to stop cybercrime. These AI-native, data-intensive SaaS applications depend on fast, reliable, and secure access to massive datasets. That’s where the Data Platform team comes in: designing and operating scalable storage systems (PostgreSQL, OpenSearch, Redis, RocksDB, DynamoDB), batch and stream data processing (Kafka, Spark), orchestration (Airflow, DBT), and more.\nWe build and maintain the core infrastructure that powers Abnormal’s most data-heavy workloads, providing scalable, reliable, and efficient data platforms and services to all of engineering and data science. We also create tools that make this infrastructure simple to operate and integrate, enabling teams to deliver faster with confidence.\nWe’re looking for a Software Engineer I who is eager to learn and ready to take on meaningful technical challenges. You’ll work alongside experienced engineers, contribute to ambitious projects, and grow your skills while helping to scale the systems that support Abnormal’s rapid growth.\nWhat You Will Do\nContribute to the design, development, and operation of core components of Abnormal’s data platform.\nBuild tools and services that make it easy for other teams to adopt and scale data systems.\nHelp automate infrastructure and operations to improve reliability, performance, and scalability.\nApply cutting-edge GenAI techniques to build smarter developer and operator experiences.\nCollaborate across engineering teams to solve scalability and reliability challenges.\nTake ownership of projects, delivering features end-to-end with guidance from senior engineers.\nWhat You Bring\n1+ years of professional experience in software engineering: backend, distributed systems, or infrastructure preferred.\nSolid programming skills in Python, Go, or a similar language (school, personal, or work experience all count).\nStrong software engineering fundamentals like data structures, clean code, testing, and debugging.\nInterest in learning about AWS, Databricks, and technologies in our stack (databases, streaming, orchestration).\nCuriosity, problem-solving skills, and a willingness to ask questions.\nAbility to work both independently and as part of a team, and strong communication skills.\nNice to Have (but you can also learn here)\nExperience with one or more of: PostgreSQL, OpenSearch/Elasticsearch, Redis, RocksDB.\nFamiliarity with cloud platforms (AWS, GCP, Azure).\nExposure to large-scale or data-intensive systems.\nWhy you’ll love it here\nYou’ll be part of a high-impact team solving problems that matter.\nYou’ll learn from and work with experienced engineers in a collaborative, supportive environment.\nYou’ll get real opportunities for ownership and career growth early in your journey.\nYou’ll help shape the future of our data platform at a fast-growing, AI-first company.\nActual compensation will be determined based on several non-discriminatory factors including skills, experience, qualifications, and geographic location.\nIn addition to base salary, this role may be eligible for bonus or incentive compensation, equity, and a comprehensive benefits package.\nBase salary range:\n$122,400—$176,000 USD\nA note on AI in our process:\nAbnormal AI uses AI-assisted tools to help our recruiting team prepare for candidate interviews. These tools analyze resume content and role requirements to suggest interview questions and areas for the interviewer to explore.They do not make hiring decisions or screen candidates automatically. Every decision about a candidacy is made by a person. Further, if your application is successful and Abnormal AI makes a conditional offer of employment, we will carry out pre-employment checks which must be successfully completed to progress to a final offer. All processes and pre-employment checks are in line with prevailing legislation and Abnormal AI's policies relevant to our security and privacy standards.\nAbnormal AI is an equal opportunity employer. Qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, national origin, disability, protected veteran status or other characteristics protected by law. For our EEO policy statement please click here . If you would like more information on your EEO rights under the law, please click here .",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4490528213": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-11-15T22:56:54.715047+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "Bright Vision Technologies is a technology consulting and software development company delivering cloud, AI, data, and enterprise solutions across the United States. This is an opportunity to contribute to technology initiatives in a collaborative environment with opportunities for professional growth.\nJob Title: React Developer\nLocation: Remote\nPosition Type: Full-time, Direct W2 - [Not open to C2C or 1099]\nSalary Range: $115,000–$165,000 Annually\nExperience Required: 4+ years\nSponsorship: U.S. Citizens, Green Card holders, EAD holders, and H-1B transfer candidates are encouraged to apply. Bright Vision Technologies is unable to sponsor new H-1B visa petitions for this position.\nJob Summary\nBright Vision Technologies is seeking a React Developer to design, develop, test, and support enterprise software applications and services using the technology stack relevant to the project. The work spans implementation, API and data integration, code quality, release readiness, and production troubleshooting. The successful candidate will apply practical expertise in React, TypeScript/JavaScript, hooks, state management, HTML, CSS, responsive design, REST/GraphQL, and front-end testing, work with cross-functional teams, and contribute to reliable, maintainable solutions through the delivery lifecycle.\nKey Responsibilities\nDesign, develop, test, and maintain application components using the approved technology stack\nTranslate functional and technical requirements into maintainable code, APIs, interfaces, or user-facing features\nIntegrate applications with databases, external services, and enterprise systems using appropriate standards\nParticipate in code reviews, automated testing, debugging, and performance improvement\nCollaborate with product, architecture, QA, and operations teams through release and production support\nRequired Qualifications\nExperience Required: typically 4+ years in a related professional role; exact threshold must match the approved requisition\nPractical experience with the role-specific technology stack: React, TypeScript/JavaScript, hooks, state management, HTML, CSS, responsive design, REST/GraphQL, and front-end testing\nProfessional experience building or supporting production software using the core technologies relevant to this role\nStrong understanding of programming fundamentals, software design, data structures, and maintainable code\nExperience with APIs, integrations, data stores, and appropriate testing practices\nWorking knowledge of Git or another source-control system and structured development workflows\nAbility to troubleshoot defects and communicate technical findings clearly\nExperience collaborating with cross-functional teams in an Agile or iterative delivery environment\nPreferred Qualifications\nAdditional hands-on depth in React, TypeScript/JavaScript, hooks, state management, HTML, CSS, responsive design, REST/GraphQL, and front-end testing\nExperience with cloud services, automation, and modern delivery practices relevant to the project\nFamiliarity with secure development, accessibility, governance, or regulatory requirements where applicable\nRelevant professional certifications or advanced training in the role’s technology area\nHow to Apply\nWould you like to know more about this opportunity? For immediate consideration, please send your resume to Hilda@bvteck.com or contact Hilda at (908) 698-4899. Learn more about Bright Vision Technologies at www.bvteck.com.\nBright Vision Technologies is an Equal Opportunity Employer.\nEqual Employment Opportunity (EEO) Statement\nBright Vision Technologies (BV Teck) is committed to equal employment opportunity (EEO) for all employees and applicants without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, national origin, age, genetic information, disability, veteran status, or any other protected status as defined by applicable federal, state, or local laws. This commitment extends to all aspects of employment, including recruitment, hiring, training, compensation, promotion, transfer, leaves of absence, termination, layoffs, and recall.\nBV Teck expressly prohibits any form of workplace harassment or discrimination. Any improper interference with employees' ability to perform their job duties may result in disciplinary action up to and including termination of employment.\nPowered by JazzHR\nsL4gQ74A9d",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4490588298": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-11-15T22:56:54.715047+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "Ability to work EST hours required!\nToast creates technology to help restaurants and local businesses succeed in a digital world, helping business owners operate, increase sales, engage customers, and keep employees happy.\nAt Toast, we are committed to empowering our customers by providing the technology, resources, and community they need to thrive. While our roots are in food service, we are rapidly expanding into adjacent markets and international territories. Our mission is to build a world-class Device Management platform that supports the diverse needs of all Toast customers, regardless of their industry or location.\nAs a frontend engineer on the Android Systems team, you will build the web experiences that sit on top of the foundational platform for Toast POS devices. Whether it’s an international team looking to deploy a new on-device application, a customer needing a critical firmware update, an Enterprise group needing multi-location device tooling - our web tools empower customers and Toast teams to set up, secure, and manage their devices from wherever they are.\nWhy this team?\nExpanding the Vision: We are expanding our Mobile Device Management ecosystem—unifying firmware, on-device apps, and security controls into one cohesive platform.\nFrictionless Device Management: We are transforming the customer’s device lifecycle experience from out-of-the-box setup to continuous remote management, leveraging AI to dramatically reduce operator’s time spent troubleshooting and configuring devices.\nAbout this roll* (Responsibilities):\nHands-on design and implementation of web applications in React and TypeScript that power Toast's device management suite, including device configuration, policy management, and firmware and app update tooling.\nCollaborate with Product Management, Hardware, QA, and other Software teams to build scalable systems, making solid technical decisions with quality, security, and maintainability in mind.\nPartner with UX to turn designs into accessible, responsive, and performant interfaces using Toast's design system.\nWrite automated unit, integration, and end-to-end tests to keep our web apps reliable as they grow.\nDeploy features out to customers using feature flags, monitor for success, and help investigate and fix production issues.\nLeverage cutting edge AI tools to enhance your development workflow, improve velocity, and help pioneer new approaches to building, contributing to a culture of innovation and productivity across the team.\nDo you have the right ingredients*? (Requirements):\n3+ years of professional frontend web development experience.\nClear written and verbal communication.\nProficient in React, TypeScript, HTML, and CSS, with experience building responsive single-page applications.\nUnderstanding of component architecture and state management.\nExperience integrating with REST or GraphQL APIs.\nExperience writing tests with frameworks such as Jest, React Testing Library, or Playwright.\nProficiency with source control and code review tools such as Git or GitHub.\nPassion for clean, maintainable code and thoughtful user experiences.\nStrong customer empathy and a drive to build tools that make restaurant operators' lives easier.\nBonus ingredients*:\nExperience working with design systems or shared component libraries.\nExperience working in large, multi-team frontend codebases or micro-frontend architectures.\nExperience with GraphQL clients and data-fetching libraries such as Apollo or React Query.\nSome backend experience in Java or Kotlin, or an interest in learning.\nInterest in hardware, Android, or mobile device management (MDM) concepts.\nFamiliarity with AI-augmented development workflows and tools (e.g., Claude Code, Codex, or similar).\nWhat we use to make our dish* (Our Tech Stack):\nReact and TypeScript micro-frontends built on Toast's in-house design system.\nGraphQL and REST APIs, using modern data-fetching and state management libraries.\nAutomated testing with Jest, React Testing Library, Storybook, and Playwright.\nKotlin backend services built on AWS that manage device policies, firmware updates, and device configuration.\nAndroid system apps in Kotlin running on Toast's POS devices.\nFeature flags and production monitoring to ship safely to customers.\nAI at Toast\nAt Toast, one of our company values is that we're hungry to build and learn. We believe learning new AI tools empowers us to build for our customers faster, more independently, and with higher quality. We provide these tools across all disciplines, from Engineering and Product to Sales and Support, and are inspired by how our Toasters are already driving real value with them. The people who thrive here are those who embrace changes that let us build more for our customers; it’s a core part of our culture.\nOur Total Rewards Philosophy\nWe strive to provide competitive compensation and benefits programs that help to attract, retain, and motivate the best and brightest people in our industry. Our total rewards package goes beyond great earnings potential and provides the means to a healthy lifestyle with the flexibility to meet Toasters’ changing needs. Learn more about our benefits at https://careers.toasttab.com/toast-benefits.\nBread puns encouraged but not required\nThe base salary range for this role is listed below. The starting salary will be determined based on skills, experience, and geographic location. In addition to base salary, our total rewards components include cash compensation (overtime, bonus/commissions if eligible), equity, and benefits. You can learn more about how we align pay with local labor markets in our Geographic Pay Zone Philosophy.\nZone A\n$133,000—$213,000 USD\nZone B\n$115,000—$184,000 USD\nZone C\n$104,000—$166,000 USD\nHow Toast Uses AI In Its Hiring Process\nThroughout the hiring process, our goal is to get to know you. We use AI tools to support our recruiters and interviewers with tasks like note-taking, summarization, and documentation of interviews to ensure they can be fully focused on your conversation. All hiring decisions are made by people. We ask that you complete interviews and assessments on your own, without real-time AI tools, recording, or transcription bots, unless we tell you otherwise in advance. To learn more: https://careers.toasttab.com/ai-in-hiring\nOur Approach to Hybrid Working\nWe embrace a hybrid work model that fosters in-person collaboration while valuing individual needs. Our goal is to build a strong culture of connection as we work together to empower the hospitality community, regardless of location. Please visit the Locations page on our career site to learn more about our in-office expectations by region: https://careers.toasttab.com/locations-toast\nPeople Are the Secret Ingredient in Our Recipe for Success\nAt Toast, our employees are our secret ingredient—when they thrive, we thrive. The restaurant industry brings together people with a wide range of backgrounds, experiences, and perspectives, and we value that same breadth at Toast. We strive to build a culture grounded in authenticity, respect, and humility, where every Toaster has a real opportunity to grow, contribute, and do their best work—raising the bar in delivering exceptional experiences for our customers and each other.\nApply today!\nToast is committed to creating an accessible and inclusive hiring process. As part of this commitment, we strive to provide reasonable accommodations for persons with disabilities to enable them to access the hiring process. If you need an accommodation to access the job application or interview process, please contact candidateaccommodations@toasttab.com.\nFor roles in the United States, it is unlawful in Massachusetts to require or administer a lie detector test as a condition of employment or continued employment. An employer who violates this law shall be subject to criminal penalties and civil liability.",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      }
    },
    "updated_at": "2026-11-15T22:56:54.715047+00:00"
  },
